It includes the third-party Rust crates listed below. Each licence is given
once per distinct text (the copyright line differs between crates), followed
by the crates it covers. Where a crate offers a choice of licences, it is
listed under the first of MIT, Apache-2.0, BSD, ISC, Zlib it allows.

Covers the macOS app and the Linux build (with Wayland screen sharing).
Generated by cargo-about from Cargo.lock; regenerate with `just notices`.

Of note: openh264 (H.264 codec, compiled from Cisco's source, BSD-2-Clause);
sonora (the WebRTC audio processing port used for echo cancellation,
BSD-3-Clause); unsafe-libopus (libopus translated to Rust, BSD-3-Clause);
aws-lc-sys (AWS-LC cryptography, ISC, Apache-2.0, MIT and BSD-3-Clause);
the ICU4X crates (Unicode-3.0).

MPL-2.0: stylo, cssparser, selectors and the other MPL-2.0 crates below are
used unmodified. Their source is published on crates.io, at the versions
listed, and in the blitz repository at tag v0.3.0-beta.4
(https://github.com/DioxusLabs/blitz), which this project builds against.

